# A snapshot of a moment, rewritten every 30 seconds by the control server.
# Never worth a merge conflict: whichever copy is newer is the right one, and
# the older one describes a state that no longer exists.
#
# `merge=ours` needs a driver registered in git config to do anything at all —
# without `merge.ours.driver`, git silently ignores it and conflicts normally,
# which is exactly what happened the first time this file met a rebase.
# `npm run sweep:share` registers it. Until then the -diff still applies, which
# keeps a binary-sized JSON blob out of every review.
evidence/snapshot.json merge=ours -diff
